Radium patch: don't construct a juce::File from an LV2 plugin URI.

LV2PluginFormat::findAllTypesForFile() is called with either an absolute path to an
LV2 bundle or with an LV2 plugin URI, such as
"http://gareus.org/oss/lv2/midifilter#mapcc" (this is what Radium's add_lv2_plugins()
passes, one container per plugin). The function passes the identifier straight to
findPluginByFile():

    for (const auto& plugin : { findPluginByUri (identifier), findPluginByFile (identifier) })

findPluginByFile() takes a const juce::File&, so the URI string is implicitly
converted to a juce::File. On macOS (and the other non-Windows platforms),
juce::File::parseAbsolutePath() calls jassertfalse() for a path that does not start
with '/' or '~'. In release builds the assert is a no-op and the resulting File
simply never matches a bundle, but in debug builds jassertfalse() aborts (Radium
patches it to abort(), see fix_jassertfalse_macro.diff), which kills the plugin
scanner process. Radium then finds no plugin descriptions for the container and
shows "Could not find a usable plugin file for <name>" for every LV2 plugin.

Fix: only look up the plugin by file when the identifier actually is an absolute
path. A plugin URI can never match a bundle path anyway.

diff --git a/pluginhost/JuceLibraryCode/modules/juce_audio_processors/format_types/juce_LV2PluginFormat.cpp b/pluginhost/JuceLibraryCode/modules/juce_audio_processors/format_types/juce_LV2PluginFormat.cpp
index 62dcd423f..b6745289e 100644
--- a/pluginhost/JuceLibraryCode/modules/juce_audio_processors/format_types/juce_LV2PluginFormat.cpp
+++ b/pluginhost/JuceLibraryCode/modules/juce_audio_processors/format_types/juce_LV2PluginFormat.cpp
@@ -5210,7 +5210,16 @@ public:
         if (File::isAbsolutePath (identifier))
             world->loadBundle (world->newFileUri (nullptr, File::addTrailingSeparator (identifier).toRawUTF8()));
 
-        for (const auto& plugin : { findPluginByUri (identifier), findPluginByFile (identifier) })
+        // Radium: The identifier is often an LV2 plugin URI (such as
+        // "http://example.com/plugin#main"), not a file path. Passing it directly to
+        // findPluginByFile() constructs a juce::File from the URI, which calls
+        // jassertfalse() (and aborts in debug builds). A URI can never match a bundle
+        // path anyway, so only look up by file when the identifier really is a path.
+        const LilvPlugin* pluginByFile = File::isAbsolutePath (identifier)
+                                           ? findPluginByFile (File (identifier))
+                                           : nullptr;
+
+        for (const auto& plugin : { findPluginByUri (identifier), pluginByFile })
         {
             if (auto desc = getDescription (plugin); desc.fileOrIdentifier.isNotEmpty())
